why 1 1/2 SIMILAR_MOTION All voices step down into iv⁶, the bass by a fifth. The phrase descends toward its cadence.
why 3 3/4 CROSS_RELATION The soprano's C♯, then C♮ in the tenor: the harmony turns from the dominant of the dominant to a diminished chord leading to A minor. The C♮ is a chromatic note in the tenor's line.
why 12 1/8 CROSS_RELATION The bass's C♯, then C♮ in the tenor: the music turns from A major color back to E minor. The C♮ belongs to the diminished seventh chord that leads there.
